{"command": "cd /testbed && mkdir -p specs/001-transactions/contracts && cat > specs/001-transactions/contracts/tagged-cache-api.md <<'EOF'\n# Contract: cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache public API\n\nPhase 1 output. This is the externally observable contract of the new\nmodule. Existing cachetools contracts (Cache, LRUCache, FIFOCache,\nLFUCache, MRUCache, RRCache, TLRUCache, TTLCache, cached, cachedmethod,\nkeys) are unchanged (Constitution Principle I).\n\n## Import\n\n```python\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\n```\n\n## Constructor\n\n```python\nTaggedCache(maxsize)\n```\n\n- maxsize: positive int, bool excluded; otherwise `ValueError` (FR-014).\n- Returns a cache with zero live entries; `len(c) == 0`, `c.maxsize ==\n  maxsize`.\n\n## put\n\n```python\nc.put(key, value, tags=())\n```\n\n- key: hashable; unhashable -> TypeError (Python contract).\n- value: any object; stored as a deep copy (FR-005). If deepcopy fails,\n  the exception propagates and prior state is unchanged (FR-015).\n- tags: default `()`; must be a finite iterable of str; not a bare str or\n  bytes; duplicate tags deduplicated; empty allowed (FR-006..FR-008).\n  Violations raise `ValueError` before any state change (FR-008).\n- Effect: inserts or replaces the entry; the entry becomes\n  most-recently-used (D2); on replacement, old tag memberships are removed\n  first (FR-010). No return value (None).\n\n## get\n\n```python\nv = c.get(key)\nv = c.get(key, default)   # inherited Cache.get\n```\n\n- Hit: returns a detached deep copy of the stored value (FR-003); entry\n  becomes most-recently-used (FR-012).\n- Miss: `c.get(key)` raises `KeyError`; `c.get(key, default)` returns\n  default (FR-004).\n\n## invalidate\n\n```python\nn = c.invalidate(tag)\n```\n\n- Removes exactly the live entries currently carrying `tag`; returns the\n  number removed (0 if none). Tag not present -> 0. (FR-009)\n\n## Inherited observable behavior (from Cache/LRUCache, unchanged)\n\n- `len(c)`: number of live entries (FR-013); never exceeds maxsize.\n- `key in c`, `iter(c)`, `c[key]` (deep-copied, KeyError on miss),\n  `c[key] = value` (plain value, no tags; refreshes recency),\n  `del c[key]`, `c.pop(key[, default])`, `c.clear()`, `c.setdefault(...)`,\n  `c.maxsize`, `c.currsize`, `c.getsizeof(value)`, `repr(c)`.\n- Every stored value costs one slot (FR-016): eviction is purely by count\n  and LRU recency, independent of value size/shape.\n\n## Error summary\n\n| Condition | Exception |\n|---|---|\n| maxsize not a positive non-bool int | ValueError |\n| tags is a bare str/bytes | ValueError |\n| any tag entry is not str | ValueError |\n| value not deepcopy-able (on put) | the deepcopy exception (e.g., TypeError) |\n| get on missing key (no default) | KeyError |\n| unhashable key | TypeError |\nEOF\necho CONTRACT_OK; wc -l specs/001-transactions/contracts/tagged-cache-api.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "CONTRACT_OK\n80 specs/001-transactions/contracts/tagged-cache-api.md\n"}